tjchen@OCF.Berkeley.EDU (Thomas Jer Chen) writes:

>Question #1:  I am wondering if there are advantageous uses of an altar
>AFTER you have turned it to your own.  Has anyone discovered a use, and
>would you please share it as a spoiler?  Thanks.

There are lots of things you can do. Among the obvious ones are:

1. #offer (fresh) corpses. If "Nothing happens" the corpse wasn't fresh.
If "you have a hopeful feeling", you cannot pray yet. If you get no
message, you can pray again. If you "see a four-leaf clover", your luck
has gone up a point. If your luck is high, and you are in favour with
your god, an object (artifact or blessed spellbook) may appear at your
feet. Your god may grant you something else, as well, like the tune to
play at the castle to lower the drawbridge.

2. Drop normal water or unholy water and #pray. If you may already
pray, you should stand on the altar and your god will change the water
to holy water. Try to change as many water into holy water at once, by
first changing your potions of sickness, hallucination and confusion
into water (#dip a non-cursed unicorn horn in them).

3. Drop ANYTHING on an alter. This will identify them as either cursed,
blessed, or uncursed.

There may be more uses to an altar, but I don't remember them just for
now.



